# Character system (design lock)

Status: **v0 + tavern recruit + office title read active** — registry + company employment + companions + generation collaborator + city tavern query/recruit + save **v6** (shared schema). Posts are **not** stored on Character. No age / tavern filters.

## Role

- Independent **character table** (`UCharacterObject` in `UCharacterManagerSubsystem`).
- Characters must be **hired by a company** before company GM / owned-fleet posts. Unowned-fleet posts (before founding) appoint from the player person + companions.
- Player has one world person (`PlayerCharacterId`); UI defaults to them.
- Founding a company auto-hires **current operated character** (this slice = player character) **and** all companions of the player person.
- **No Family module** — do not reintroduce.

## Architecture

| Piece | Path / type |
|-------|-------------|
| Object | `UCharacterObject` — `Source/.../Character/` |
| Manager | `UCharacterManagerSubsystem` |
| Generation | `UCharacterGeneration` (collaborator, Outer = manager; **not** a new system folder) |
| Settings | `UCharacterManagerSettings` (avatar **folders**, NPC seeds, `TavernPoolSize`) |
| Types | `CharacterTypes.h` (`Char_PlayerLeader`, `Char_Gen_*`, generate request) |
| UI | `UCharacterPanelWidget` / list row → SimHud; city tavern `UCityTavernWidget` under city panel |
| Save | `FCharacterSaveData` in `SaveTypes.h` (schema **v6**; character POD still has no post fields — `HostCityId` / `LeaderCharacterId` from v4) |

Logic only — **no scene Actor / mesh** for individuals (see **`character-visual-policy.mdc`**).

## Scene & agency (lock)

Summary — full policy: **`character-visual-policy.mdc`**.

| Rule | Lock |
|------|------|
| Visual | **No individual 3D mesh or skeletal animation** for `Char_*`. Identity = **avatar icon** (UI) + text. |
| Strategic map | Characters are **never** independent person Actors. No walk / patrol as a person mesh. |
| Where they “are” | **Logic only** — employed/serving on a fleet, city, or other logic host (office/post). **Not** on the 3D ship mesh. |
| Ship posts (UI) | In-port **改装**: **2D ship diagram** + **avatar icon** per `OutfitSlot_*` — see `ship-system.mdc` **Outfit schematic**. |
| How they act on the map | Through the **host** they operate. At sea: the **fleet** moves, patrols, fights, trades. |
| Crowd / army 3D | Illustrative **mass** only — undecided, may never ship — see **`character-visual-policy.mdc`**. |
| Overturn | Explicit Ruida decision + update **`character-visual-policy.mdc`** and this section. |

## Fleet command vs other posts

- **All** fleet gameplay actions (sail, attack, trade with fleets/cities, patrol, …) are issued under the **舰队司令** (`EFleetPost` Commander) of that fleet.
- **Unrelated:** any future **ship-level 舰长** (ship system may not exist), and **other fleet office holders** (水手长 / 炮长 / 领航员, …). Those posts do not authorize fleet-level orders.
- Character module does not store posts on `UCharacterObject`; occupants live on Company / Fleet — see `fleet-system.mdc` / company office rules.

## Ids

- Form: `Char_<Name>`. Player seed: **`Char_PlayerLeader`**. Generated pool: **`Char_Gen_1`**…
- Collision: append numeric suffix (`Char_Foo_2`).
- Category: `"Character"` / `"Character|…"`.

## Fields (runtime)

| Field | Meaning |
|-------|---------|
| `CompanyId` | Employer; `None` = unemployed |
| `HostCityId` | City tavern this unemployed hanger is in; cleared on recruit |
| `LeaderCharacterId` | Companion of that character; `None` = not a companion. Cleared when hired into a company |

Posts are **not** fields on `UCharacterObject`. UI reads a display title from Company + Fleets (`GetCharacterOfficeTitle`). Owner identity is not a job slot and may combine with GM / fleet posts (e.g. `所有者；舰队司令`).

## Employment

- Character.`CompanyId` + Company.`EmployeeCharacterIds` (kept in sync via `HireCharacterToCompany` / `ClearCharacterEmployment`).
- Hire also clears `HostCityId` and `LeaderCharacterId`.
- **Cannot hire another company's owner** (`OwnerCharacterId`) into a different company.
- After save Apply: `SyncCompanyEmployeeListsFromCharacters()` rebuilds company lists from Character.`CompanyId`.
- Dismiss: **Company** `DismissEmployee` (company panel employee list). Not on Character UI.

## Companions

- **Not** a proto-company. New game still has **no** `Company_Player`.
- Companion hangs on the character: `LeaderCharacterId` (player tavern recruits → `PlayerCharacterId`).
- Found company: hire current operated character **plus** `HirePlayerCompanionsIntoCompany()` (all `Leader == PlayerCharacterId`), then Leader is cleared.
- NPC-captain crews: **not this slice**. Seeded NPC **company starter fleets** + **fleet command AI** (state machine, host-budget) — see `npc-ai.mdc`.

## Generation

- Lives in Character module (`UCharacterGeneration`). Main path = **rules inside the module**.
- **Temp rule (this slice):** new game / `ResetToBootstrap`, **after** city tavern facilities exist: create **exactly `TavernPoolSize` (default 10)** unemployed NPCs. Each independently assigned to a **random city that has a Tavern**. Some taverns 0, some many.
- Important `NpcSeeds` are **not** in that 10 and **default not in taverns**.
- Entities live **only** in the Character registry. Tavern facility stores **no roster**.
- **When:** bootstrap / Reset — **not** on opening tavern.
- **Special path:** `RequestGenerateCharacters` (tavern / events). Uncommon. **City tavern UI must not call it.**
- Generated display names: placeholder `旅人 N`. Avatars from NPC folder pick.
- Save Apply **does not** re-run the temp pool.

## Tavern query / recruit

Query “people in this tavern”: `HostCityId == city` AND `CompanyId` none AND `LeaderCharacterId` none AND not the player character.

Recruit:

- No company → companion of the player person (`LeaderCharacterId = PlayerCharacterId`), clear `HostCityId`.
- Has company → `HireCharacterToCompany(..., Company_Player)` (clears host + leader).
- After recruit they disappear from that city’s tavern list.

## Bootstrap

- New game / Initialize: seed player stub + important NPCs, then temp tavern pool. Company module then hires important NPC seeds into NPC companies; Fleet/Company seed one starter fleet per NPC company.
- Character `Initialize` **depends on Facility** (Facility already depends on City).
- Player creation UI (between new game and map): **later**; temporary seed for now.
- Avatar: pick once from **content folders** at seed; **persist in save**; NPC folder scan excludes player avatar path.
- Configure folders in **Project Settings → Game → Character Manager**.

